Title
Library Management System


Problem Statement
Traditional library management is often performed manually, which can lead to errors in book records, delays in issuing and returning books, difficulty tracking borrowed books, and increased administrative workload. A digital Library Management System is needed to automate these processes, improve efficiency, and provide accurate record management.


Objectives
Automate library operations.
Maintain book and student records efficiently.
Simplify book issue and return processes.
Reduce manual errors.
Provide quick search and retrieval of book information.
Send notifications for due dates and reminders.
Generate reports for library management.

Modules
1. User Authentication Module
User login and authentication
Role-based access control
2. Book Management Module
Add new books
Update book details
Delete books
Search books
3. Student Management Module
Add student records
Update student information
View student details
4. Book Issue & Return Module
Issue books to students
Return borrowed books
Track due dates
5. Barcode Management Module
Generate barcode for books
Scan barcode for quick operations
6. Notification Module
Email reminders
Due date notifications
7. Reports Module
Issue history reports
Return history reports
Inventory reports
System Modules Table
Module	Description
